# Presentation-golden corpus manifest.
#
# One row per bk2 sample set. presentation-corpus.sh captures, for each bk2,
# a canonical leg (tick-keyed) and an intermediate leg (deterministic alpha=0.5,
# VBL-keyed) on the native -vk path under llvmpipe. See
# notes/plans/openpete-presentation-golden.md.
#
# Fields (pipe-separated):
#   name      bk2 basename under games/spyro-1/bk2/ (its .args sidecar is
#             auto-spliced by the binary, so --skip-to-level etc. need not be
#             repeated here)
#   start     first VBL frame to sample: the first frame %interval==0 AFTER the
#             level finishes loading (g_Gamestate 0x800757D8 -> GS_Playing (0)
#             PLUS the fade-in settle). Verify the first sample isn't a
#             fade/transition frame (color-count or eyeball) when adding a bk2.
#   interval  optional VBL spacing (default 100). The canonical leg samples
#             start, start+interval, … ; the intermediate (alpha=0.5) leg samples
#             start+interval/2, … — both up to the movie's last input frame.
#
# The frame-limit and both sample grids are DERIVED from the bk2's own length
# (the input-frame count in its Input Log.txt): each grid extends to the first
# point PAST the last input frame (canonical %interval, intermediate the +half
# offset), so the final settled frame after the movie is captured, and the run
# goes to there. Nothing here is tied to a bk2's duration except its load-aligned
# start. (cliff-town-vista: movie 4911 → canonical …4900,5000 / intermediate
# …4850,4950; frame-limit 5001.)
#
# Bring-up is a single bk2 (cliff-town-vista, a far-terrain vista that exercises
# the depth fix's far-precision risk): loads at f1197, GS_Playing at f1584,
# fade settles ~f1650 → start f1700; the movie is 4911 input frames. Widen the
# set only once the pipeline is trusted end-to-end (plan fan-out item).
#
# name              | start | interval
cliff-town-vista    | 1700  | 100
